{"id":"000VXJ","title":"Lily Labyrinth","author":"dawsonjones2020","solvedCount":1,"difficulty":2,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-07T16:53:08+00:00","posted":"Heute, 16:03 Uhr","rules":"I’ve been down the yttrio rabbit hole lately (haven’t we all?), and came across a pencil puzzle genre I hadn’t seen before: Firefly. It immediately sparked several ideas for incorporating its rules into Sudoku. This puzzle is the first in a series exploring those ideas. I hope you enjoy! If you do, feel free to leave a comment and check out my other puzzles!\n\nSolve on SudokuPad\n\nRules\n\nFirefly: For each circle, draw a path starting from its gray dot, moving through the centers of cells, and ending at a circle (potentially the same one it started at), but not on the side containing another gray dot. Paths may not cross themselves, each other, or pass through circles. A number in a circle represents how many turns the path exiting from its dot will make. All circles must be joined by paths to form one connected network.\n\nChaos Construction: Divide the grid into six orthogonally connected regions of six cells. Each row, column and region contains the digits 1–6 once each. Each region contains exactly one circle. A path may only cross a region boundary on its final step into its ending circle.\n\nAmbiguous Kropki Dots: The gray dots in the grid represent either white kropki dots or black kropki dots, to be determined by the solver. White kropki dots join consecutive digits. Black kropki dots join digits in a 2:1 ratio.","solutionCode":"Row 3, with \"-\" for region borders","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/zw17pnnu2g","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/zw17pnnu2g","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":6,"cols":6,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-07T16:53:08+00:00"}